abstract:
Real data overlaps, so the hard margin is infeasible. Slack variables let points violate the margin at a price, and $C$ sets that price. We derive the soft-margin primal and dual, show that it is exactly hinge loss plus L2 regularisation, classify the three kinds of support vector by their $\alpha_i$, and measure how $C$ moves the model along the bias–variance curve.}
